# wear/man/apron: the man's work apron (smith, shipwright, innkeeper): a leather bib over a linen work shirt, the neck
# loop beside the open collar, a stitched chest pocket, a dark tool belt with a brass buckle, the skirt to mid-thigh
# (apron_hang); from behind the straps cross over the shirt to the waist tie and its knot. Sleeves rolled to the elbow
# (sleeve_rolled_*). GARB-M (P2b wave 2); fitted to the man (STYLE_P2 22). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# Build masks: broad widens the shoulder row under the arms (the arms stay at their anchors); slim and broad move the
# back in side views.
# The side run (leg pass round 2, 2026-10-20): the side `run` views are the rest views with the first row under the
# belt dropped, so the hem rides a row up while running (the skirt flaring) and the legs show under it as limbs.
# The motion rebuild (2026-10-21): the side `run` views' last rows reach a pixel further back (the walking and running
# legs' seat, the run's lean) so no sliver of leg shows behind the hem.
# PROTO6 i3 (2026-10-22; the blind panel: the run read as an upright walk): each side `run` view has a `runl` twin that
# the side run frames name (loco.clip torso=runl): the rows from 4 under the neck sit a pixel back and from 7 under it two
# pixels back, so under the clip's lean 4 the chest leads the waist (a real lean; the head never leaves the torso) and the
# hem lands where lean 2 put it, over the run legs; the hip-anchored tails follow it (hip 2, the woman's 3). Walks keep `run`.
use person woman
legend Z linen 4
body man
role garment apron
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso

